 "traps": [
  "pyproject.toml declares its dependencies as dynamic: a custom Hatch hook (scripts/packaging/hatch_metadata.py) reads them from requirements.txt, so the frameworks are in requirements.txt",
  "the Python project and netbox/project-static/package.json are both named netbox, so their frameworks are attributed by root; netbox-graphiql is a yarn workspace member with React",
  "PostgreSQL is the only database: settings.py fills in the postgresql engine when configuration.py gives none; Redis is required for tasks and caching",
  "there is no compose file: every service comes from netbox/netbox/configuration_example.py, settings.py or an optional extra (ldap, saml2, s3, swift, sentry) of pyproject.toml",
  "NetBox Census, the plugin catalog and NetBox Copilot are NetBox Labs endpoints hard-coded in settings.py",
  "social login uses social-auth-app-django with the backend chosen in configuration, so no provider is fixed; tests use Django's test runner, not pytest",
  "only frameworks and services are measured; the other facets are in unknown"
 ],
